    "ledger": [
      {
        "id": "E1",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "ALTK-Evolve: How learned memory tops the τ²-bench leaderboard on customer service tasks without a frontier model",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "ALTK-Evolve learns and applies a playbook using GPT-4.1, outperforming the retail entries on τ²-bench, a customer service agent benchmark—without updating model weights.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Learned memory takes a basic ReAct agent with GPT-4.1 to the top",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Using GPT-4.1, an older, non-reasoning model, a basic customer-service agent reaches 67.5% Pass^4 on τ²-bench retail — meaning it solves the task on all four independent attempts for 67.5% of tasks.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We run τ²-bench's own implementation of a basic ReAct agent with a two-phase THINK → ACT loop, using gpt-4.1 as the agent model and gpt-5.5 as the customer-simulator model; 4 trials per task.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We extract guidelines from the agent's trajectories on τ²-bench train tasks using gpt-4.1 , the same model that powers the agent, then apply them unchanged on the held-out test set.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "A fair objection is that learned guidelines might have less to add to an agent using a frontier model: maybe they only patch the gaps of a weaker model.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On the same held-out test tasks, appending them to the prompt lifts accuracy +10 pts (72.5 → 82.5) and the strict Pass^4 by +15 pts (55.0 → 70.0) — a larger reliability gain than we observed with gpt-4.1 on these very tasks (+10 pts), and from a much higher floor.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On the base split the agent with learned guidelines reaches Pass^4 = 67.5% , ahead of every frontier model and ahead of RAFT-30B-A3B (61.4%), a model fine-tuned on synthetic τ²-bench retail data .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Swap in the stronger base and the same approach tops the field outright: the agent using gpt-5.5 reaches 82.0% , clearing every frontier entry (66–72%).",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Pass^4 comparison between ALTK-Evolve runs and the τ²-bench leaderboard snapshot from October 12, 2026.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-21T15:10:14.697Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Same message in both domains: learning guidelines around the model works across different base models — bringing an agent using an older, non-reasoning model into frontier company on retail, and taking an agent using a frontier model to the top on airline.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://huggingface.co/blog/ibm-research/altk-evolve-bc",
        "source": "Hugging Face Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-20T15:19:48.000Z",
